                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The worldbuilding is very, very good. The world has a lot of unspoken history, only seen in far off ancient monuments or descriptions of places on the map. Very Tolkien-esque.\n\nThe story is really compelling, and had me gripped pretty much from the beginning. The last third of the game I competed in one sitting, I couldn't put it down as the stakes got higher and higher.\n\nThe combat isn't my absolute favourite ever, but it's very much well thought out and does have some super satisfying moments. It's tactical and does require a lot of thought at times, if you rush things the game won't hesistate to ruin your day. \n\n9/10",
                        "timestamp_created": 1793620717,
